.TH "RAPTOR-EXPLAIN" 1 "2026-10" "RAPTOR Studio" "RAPTOR Studio Manual"
.SH NAME
raptor\-explain \- Run MODEL and attribute every system outage to the element that started it and to a cause: hands\-on repair, waiting for a spare, waiting for people or equipment, logistics delay, planned maintenance, or being held by another element. Shows each element's share of system downtime (with its sampling error), of outages and of failures, and what typical outages look like. The engine's results are unchanged: this replays the event log.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBraptor explain\fR [\-h] [\-n N] [\-j N] [\-\-seed N] [\-\-analysis LIST] [\-\-importance MODE] [\-\-top N] [\-\-yearly] [\-\-year\-length T] [\-\-year\-offset T] [\-\-below A] [\-\-capacity\-rule {proportional,marginal,first_failed}] [\-\-report PATH] [\-\-report\-include LIST] [\-\-story] [\-\-chart NAME] [\-\-chart\-svg PATH] [\-\-chart\-page {screen,slide,a4,a3}] [\-\-chart\-min\-share S] [\-\-chart\-run N] [\-\-y\-floor F] [\-\-list\-charts] [\-\-progress {auto,bar,json,none}] [\-f {text,json}] [MODEL]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run MODEL and attribute every system outage to the element that started it and to a cause: hands\-on repair, waiting for a spare, waiting for people or equipment, logistics delay, planned maintenance, or being held by another element. Shows each element's share of system downtime (with its sampling error), of outages and of failures, and what typical outages look like. The engine's results are unchanged: this replays the event log.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Options
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-runs\fR \fIN\fR
number of runs (default: the model's own)
.TP
\fB\-j\fR, \fB\-\-jobs\fR \fIN\fR
worker processes (default 1; more is reproducible but gives different numbers from \-j 1)
.TP
\fB\-\-seed\fR \fIN\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-analysis\fR \fILIST\fR
weak,cost,capacity for this run (replaces the model's setting; the file is untouched): the cost and lost\-capacity charts need them
.TP
\fB\-\-importance\fR \fIMODE\fR
also estimate importance measures: improvement, risk or both (importance\-quadrant needs both); one extra batch per block, two for both
.TP
\fB\-\-top\fR \fIN\fR
how many elements to list (default 10)
.TP
\fB\-\-yearly\fR
also slice availability by period (a year when the model's unit is hours) and give percentiles: what a bad year looks like
.TP
\fB\-\-year\-length\fR \fIT\fR
period length in the model's time unit (implies \-\-yearly)
.TP
\fB\-\-year\-offset\fR \fIT\fR
where the first period starts (default 0)
.TP
\fB\-\-below\fR \fIA\fR
report the share of periods with availability below A, e.g. 0.97 (implies \-\-yearly)
.TP
\fB\-\-capacity\-rule\fR \fI{proportional|marginal|first_failed}\fR
how to share a capacity\-analysis run's lost flow among the elements that were down (default proportional)
.TP
\fB\-\-report\fR \fIPATH\fR
also write the report for a reader who wants the answer: PATH.pdf or one self\-contained PATH.html (the GUI's File > Export PDF)
.TP
\fB\-\-report\-include\fR \fILIST\fR
report sections, comma separated, from diagram, story, results (every result table) and data_tables (default diagram,story)
.TP
\fB\-\-story\fR
print the Story: headline against target, distribution, drivers, findings and key numbers
.TP
\fB\-\-chart\fR \fINAME\fR
also build one chart from this run, e.g. downtime\-pareto or availability\-ladder (see \-\-list\-charts)
.TP
\fB\-\-chart\-svg\fR \fIPATH\fR
write the chart as SVG (implies \-\-chart when it is missing)
.TP
\fB\-\-chart\-page\fR \fI{screen|slide|a4|a3}\fR
page the SVG is drawn for: a bigger page gives long names more room; slide, a4 and a3 also set the physical size (default screen, 760 x 400)
.TP
\fB\-\-chart\-min\-share\fR \fIS\fR
fold the items below this share of the whole (0 to 1, e.g. 0.01) into one 'N others' row or cell; rankings and treemaps only
.TP
\fB\-\-chart\-run\fR \fIN\fR
the run a one\-run chart over time shows (availability\-through\-run, interval\-availability, capacity\-through\-run; default 1)
.TP
\fB\-\-y\-floor\fR \fIF\fR
lower limit of an availability chart over time, 0 to 1 (default: fitted to the data)
.TP
\fB\-\-list\-charts\fR
list the chart names and exit
.TP
\fB\-\-progress\fR \fI{auto|bar|json|none}\fR
progress on stderr: set\-up, replications and the attribution replay (json: one object per line)
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR \fI{text|json}\fR

.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Run the model and list what causes its downtime, by element and by cause.
.RS
.nf
\fBraptor explain plant.rbds\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
500 runs on four cores; the five largest contributors.
.RS
.nf
\fBraptor explain plant.rbds \-n 500 \-j 4 \-\-top 5\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
Also availability year by year with percentiles, and how often a year falls below 97 %.
.RS
.nf
\fBraptor explain plant.rbds \-\-yearly \-\-below 0.97\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
The full attribution, machine\-readable.
.RS
.nf
\fBraptor explain plant.rbds \-f json\fR
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBraptor\fR(1)
